WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.234
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.828
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.128 --> 00:00:14.729
Unit nineteen: Part-Time Jobs. Today you will talk about possibilities with could.

4
00:00:15.029 --> 00:00:17.681
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.633 --> 00:00:21.866
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.717 --> 00:00:24.205
Part-time job.

7
00:00:25.217 --> 00:00:28.772
Part-time job means a job for only some hours each week.

8
00:00:29.383 --> 00:00:32.207
My brother has a part-time job at a café.

9
00:00:32.817 --> 00:00:35.957
Your turn. Say: Part-time job.

10
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.115
Part-time job.

11
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:41.874
Employer.

12
00:00:42.883 --> 00:00:46.206
Employer means a person or company that pays workers.

13
00:00:46.817 --> 00:00:48.805
My employer is very kind.

14
00:00:49.417 --> 00:00:51.906
Your turn. Say: Employer.

15
00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:55.884
Employer.

16
00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:57.489
Wage.

17
00:00:58.483 --> 00:01:01.818
Wage means money you earn for work, often by the hour.

18
00:01:02.417 --> 00:01:04.161
The wage is two dollars an hour.

19
00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.822
Your turn. Say: Wage.

20
00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:10.691
Wage.

21
00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:12.927
Responsibility.

22
00:01:13.917 --> 00:01:16.961
Responsibility means a duty to do something well.

23
00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.956
Opening the shop is my responsibility.

24
00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:23.899
Your turn. Say: Responsibility.

25
00:01:26.733 --> 00:01:28.338
Responsibility.

26
00:01:29.083 --> 00:01:30.363
Experience.

27
00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:34.151
Experience means knowledge you get from doing things.

28
00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.051
Work experience helps you get a job.

29
00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:40.720
Your turn. Say: Experience.

30
00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:45.044
Experience.

31
00:01:45.783 --> 00:01:46.657
Schedule.

32
00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:50.451
Schedule means a plan of times for activities.

33
00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:53.398
My work schedule changes every week.

34
00:01:53.983 --> 00:01:56.357
Your turn. Say: Schedule.

35
00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.155
Schedule.

36
00:02:00.917 --> 00:02:01.662
Shift.

37
00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:04.998
Shift means a period of time when you work.

38
00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:07.803
I work the evening shift on Saturdays.

39
00:02:08.417 --> 00:02:10.512
Your turn. Say: Shift.

40
00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:14.054
Shift.

41
00:02:14.817 --> 00:02:15.609
Skill.

42
00:02:16.617 --> 00:02:19.266
Skill means an ability you get by practice.

43
00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:22.256
Serving customers is a useful skill.

44
00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.247
Your turn. Say: Skill.

45
00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:29.031
Skill.

46
00:02:29.833 --> 00:02:33.322
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:34.183 --> 00:02:36.554
Visal, would you like a part-time job?

48
00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:40.987
Yes! Maybe at my uncle's phone shop.

49
00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:43.259
What could you learn?

50
00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:48.567
A part-time job could teach me responsibility and customer skills.

51
00:02:49.683 --> 00:02:51.184
What about school?

52
00:02:52.283 --> 00:02:56.942
I could work a short shift on weekends, so my schedule stays balanced.

53
00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.844
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:00.683 --> 00:03:03.612
Grammar focus: Modal 'could' for possibility.

55
00:03:03.912 --> 00:03:05.110
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:05.817 --> 00:03:08.757
A part-time job could teach you responsibility.

57
00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:11.023
You could earn a wage.

58
00:03:11.917 --> 00:03:13.789
It could help your future career.

59
00:03:14.733 --> 00:03:17.801
'Could' shows that something is possible, but not certain.

60
00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:23.675
Be careful! Don't say: A part-time job could teaches you responsibility.

61
00:03:25.633 --> 00:03:29.189
Say: A part-time job could teach you responsibility.

62
00:03:29.489 --> 00:03:31.511
After 'could', use the base verb.

63
00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:34.778
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:35.567 --> 00:03:36.962
My First Job.

65
00:03:37.262 --> 00:03:40.446
Having a part-time job teaches responsibility.

66
00:03:41.433 --> 00:03:43.630
It gives you real work experience.

67
00:03:44.633 --> 00:03:47.631
You learn to manage your schedule around your work shift.

68
00:03:48.633 --> 00:03:52.119
You earn a wage, and your employer helps you learn new skills.

69
00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:56.247
A part-time job could help you choose a future career.

70
00:03:57.333 --> 00:04:01.405
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:04.772
A job blank teach you responsibility.

72
00:04:05.072 --> 00:04:08.667
A, could. B, coulds. C, could to.

73
00:04:12.233 --> 00:04:13.850
The answer is A: could.

74
00:04:14.983 --> 00:04:17.122
Money you earn for work is a blank.

75
00:04:17.422 --> 00:04:20.716
A, wage. B, shift. C, skill.

76
00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:25.999
The answer is A: wage.

77
00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:29.370
A period of time when you work is a blank.

78
00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:33.115
A, shift. B, schedule. C, employer.

79
00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:38.655
The answer is A: shift.

80
00:04:39.867 --> 00:04:43.227
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:47.290
What skills do you think a part-time job could teach you?

82
00:04:56.083 --> 00:04:57.549
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:57.849 --> 00:05:04.658
A part-time job could teach me how to talk to customers and handle money. It could also teach me time management.

84
00:05:04.958 --> 00:05:06.725
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:07.617 --> 00:05:11.952
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and modal 'could' for possibility.

86
00:05:12.252 --> 00:05:16.275
Today's value is responsibility. Help at home and do your jobs.

87
00:05:16.575 --> 00:05:19.215
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

88
00:05:19.515 --> 00:05:22.272
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

